    "updated_at": "2024-05-17T21:13:41Z",
    "body": "Ah ok, I can see that calling element.click() on `<input type=color>` currently opens the picker, so if we made it check for and consume user activation, that could be a breaking change. Calling element.click() on `<select>` doesn't seem to currently do anything though.\r\n\r\nI think it would probably be a good idea to make that require user activation though since it opens a popup document. I can guard the change behind a flag and revert it if websites are relying too much on it or something.\r\n\r\nLet's do it!\r\n\r\nThe WPT should probably test the element.click() cases, right? This algorithm does get called when doing element.click(), right?",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/2118390807/reactions",
